1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:01,000
(All characters, locations,
and events are fictional

2
00:00:01,025 --> 00:00:02,158
and for entertainment
purposes only.

3
00:00:02,182 --> 00:00:03,166
No actions depicted are intended
to be encouraged or endorsed.

4
00:00:03,191 --> 00:00:04,635
Animals were specially trained
and supervised by professionals.

5
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:05,697
Viewer discretion is advised.)

6
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:17,957
A golf course may seem
peaceful and perfectly ordered.

7
00:00:17,982 --> 00:00:21,749
But who knows what lies
beneath that pristine green?

8
00:00:21,829 --> 00:00:27,383
Pressure, expectations,
and the dreams of so many people.

9
00:00:27,447 --> 00:00:30,005
Golf isn't about competing
against someone else.

10
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:32,605
It's about competing
against yourself.

11
00:00:32,630 --> 00:00:35,884
Every shot takes thought.
Every swing, a decision.

12
00:00:36,030 --> 00:00:39,500
And every mistake
is something you have to accept.

13
00:00:39,525 --> 00:00:41,344
A fairway may look smooth,

14
00:00:41,369 --> 00:00:43,552
but that doesn't mean
there won't be obstacles ahead.

15
00:00:43,577 --> 00:00:46,967
Relationships on this course
are no different.

16
00:00:46,992 --> 00:00:49,369
Some come back out of duty.

17
00:00:49,402 --> 00:00:52,035
Some stay to chase their dreams.

18
00:00:52,409 --> 00:00:54,666
And some don't even realize

19
00:00:54,691 --> 00:00:57,843
they're about to fall in love.

20
00:00:58,098 --> 00:01:01,735
Because in golf,
no one wins alone.

21
00:01:01,927 --> 00:01:05,796
And in love,
no one makes it to the finish

22
00:01:05,821 --> 00:01:09,456
without someone
to play the course by their side.

23
00:01:18,360 --> 00:01:21,718
♪ Everyone can tell
by the way you stare ♪

24
00:01:22,457 --> 00:01:24,180
♪ Sneaking little looks
when I'm unaware ♪

25
00:01:24,205 --> 00:01:28,374
♪ It's plain to see ♪

26
00:01:28,399 --> 00:01:29,973
♪ I know exactly
what you think of me ♪

27
00:01:29,998 --> 00:01:33,301
♪ First to watch my stories
every time ♪

28
00:01:34,144 --> 00:01:35,827
♪ You remember
every fave of mine ♪

29
00:01:35,852 --> 00:01:39,585
♪ Everywhere I go,
you're by my side ♪

30
00:01:39,610 --> 00:01:41,621
♪ Don't tell me
there's nothing on your mind ♪

31
00:01:41,646 --> 00:01:44,337
♪ So when are you
gonna say the words? ♪

32
00:01:44,536 --> 00:01:46,387
♪ Don't keep me waiting
till it hurts ♪

33
00:01:46,412 --> 00:01:49,143
♪ The way you act,
I know you're into me ♪

34
00:01:49,168 --> 00:01:52,139
♪ That racing heart
gives you away so easily ♪

35
00:01:52,164 --> 00:01:55,976
♪ But I'll play clueless,
just wait and see ♪

36
00:01:56,001 --> 00:01:58,001
♪ I wanna hear you say it to me ♪

37
00:01:58,026 --> 00:02:00,910
♪ Giving me signs,
so why still wait? ♪

38
00:02:00,935 --> 00:02:04,342
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

39
00:02:04,367 --> 00:02:09,083
♪ How long will you keep
playing so tough? ♪

40
00:02:09,108 --> 00:02:10,958
♪ Or should I be the one
to call your bluff? ♪

41
00:03:10,974 --> 00:03:13,312
Miss! Miss Nana!

42
00:03:14,481 --> 00:03:15,600
Queen?

43
00:03:18,330 --> 00:03:19,829
Is that you, Queen?

44
00:03:19,956 --> 00:03:25,235
It's Chef Queen now.

45
00:03:25,642 --> 00:03:28,495
Oh! Have you seen Dad?

46
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:31,505
He's out playing. He should be
on the last hole by now.

47
00:03:31,530 --> 00:03:33,785
Why don't you wait
in the lounge, Miss Nana?

48
00:03:33,810 --> 00:03:35,193
Your father should be back soon.

49
00:03:35,218 --> 00:03:38,441
No. I need to see Dad. Now!

50
00:03:39,270 --> 00:03:42,209
Wow? I know, you look fabulous.

51
00:03:42,280 --> 00:03:45,902
No! I mean, now. Right now.
This instant.

52
00:03:45,927 --> 00:03:49,928
Now. This instant.
Right now. Go, go, go!

53
00:03:49,953 --> 00:03:51,770
Driver! Bring me
the best cart you've got.

54
00:03:51,795 --> 00:03:53,423
Something that starts
on the first try.

55
00:03:53,447 --> 00:03:55,017
None of that
chug-chug-chug nonsense!

56
00:03:55,042 --> 00:03:56,597
The boss should be
on the last hole.

57
00:03:56,621 --> 00:03:58,940
We'll track him down. Let's go!

58
00:04:10,986 --> 00:04:12,441
- Hey, March.
- Yes, Uncle?

59
00:04:12,751 --> 00:04:15,259
I saw last
quarter's financial report.

60
00:04:15,689 --> 00:04:17,291
The numbers don't look too good.

61
00:04:17,894 --> 00:04:18,926
I know, Uncle.

62
00:04:19,113 --> 00:04:21,817
I'm doing everything I can to get
us back to where we used to be.

63
00:04:23,374 --> 00:04:26,101
I understand. Golfers have
a lot more options these days.

64
00:04:26,610 --> 00:04:28,875
But if things keep going
like this...

65
00:04:29,463 --> 00:04:31,426
I think I may have to...

66
00:04:31,608 --> 00:04:33,067
Don't worry, Uncle.

67
00:04:33,092 --> 00:04:36,306
I've got a new plan to put
our course back on the map.

68
00:04:37,391 --> 00:04:41,392
Is it actually a new plan,
or last month's with a new title?

69
00:04:41,417 --> 00:04:43,910
And a new cover, right, March?

70
00:04:47,422 --> 00:04:49,147
All right,
let's finish the game first.

71
00:05:01,186 --> 00:05:06,044
Look, I just want us
to try something new.

72
00:05:06,601 --> 00:05:09,207
A new idea, a new approach,
anything.

73
00:05:09,232 --> 00:05:11,232
Something different
from what we've always done.

74
00:05:18,149 --> 00:05:19,305
Dad!

75
00:05:27,031 --> 00:05:28,402
You made me come all the way back

76
00:05:28,427 --> 00:05:29,934
when I was this close

77
00:05:29,959 --> 00:05:31,934
to working for every fashion
grad's dream brand.

78
00:05:31,958 --> 00:05:33,702
Was it really that urgent?

79
00:05:34,742 --> 00:05:36,449
Well, you've graduated,
haven't you?

80
00:05:38,022 --> 00:05:39,208
Yes, I have.

81
00:05:39,233 --> 00:05:41,788
But I'm applying for internships
with global brands over there.

82
00:05:41,813 --> 00:05:44,562
The reason I called you home

83
00:05:45,201 --> 00:05:47,613
is because I don't want
the golf course

84
00:05:47,638 --> 00:05:49,462
falling into
someone else's hands.

85
00:05:49,905 --> 00:05:51,008
What do you mean?

86
00:05:51,930 --> 00:05:53,846
The course is about
to go under, Nana.

87
00:05:54,150 --> 00:05:56,467
Wow. Thank you,
my darling August,

88
00:05:56,538 --> 00:05:59,121
for that wonderfully concise
and crystal-clear explanation.

89
00:05:59,518 --> 00:06:00,605
Wow.

90
00:06:03,149 --> 00:06:05,302
It's not quite that bad, Nana.

91
00:06:05,910 --> 00:06:08,949
I'm working on a turnaround plan

92
00:06:08,974 --> 00:06:10,465
to make the course
profitable again.

93
00:06:10,709 --> 00:06:14,199
- It's just that...
- It's just that March's plans

94
00:06:14,224 --> 00:06:17,430
have been sending our revenue
backwards every single month.

95
00:06:19,282 --> 00:06:21,520
If it's not working,
just sell it.

96
00:06:21,545 --> 00:06:23,227
Our family has plenty of
other businesses.

97
00:06:23,295 --> 00:06:25,468
How can you say that so casually?

98
00:06:25,493 --> 00:06:28,112
Your grandfather
loved this course.

99
00:06:28,518 --> 00:06:30,495
I know. But if it can't survive,

100
00:06:30,520 --> 00:06:31,957
why keep it, Dad?

101
00:06:32,067 --> 00:06:35,245
It was the first business
your grandfather ever built,

102
00:06:35,270 --> 00:06:36,906
before he started all the others.

103
00:06:36,931 --> 00:06:38,909
But Grandpa's not here anymore.

104
00:06:39,039 --> 00:06:40,045
Hey...

105
00:06:40,069 --> 00:06:42,991
But his name
is still our family name.

106
00:06:43,016 --> 00:06:46,249
It'd be like we couldn't even
preserve what our family built.

107
00:06:48,449 --> 00:06:50,208
Then why don't you help?

108
00:06:50,233 --> 00:06:53,265
***You know what they say.
When in Rome, lend a hand.

109
00:06:53,290 --> 00:06:54,664
- Huh?
- What?

110
00:06:54,782 --> 00:06:56,483
Is that even a saying?

111
00:06:57,047 --> 00:07:01,516
It's "When in Rome,
do as the Romeos do."

112
00:07:01,541 --> 00:07:04,427
And I'm not "in Rome," Nana,
so that doesn't even apply.

113
00:07:04,452 --> 00:07:07,923
Besides, I've been helping
as much as I can.

114
00:07:10,119 --> 00:07:12,349
Oh, come on.
August just started college.

115
00:07:12,374 --> 00:07:15,351
- He's not quite there yet.
- Excuse me?

116
00:07:15,457 --> 00:07:19,179
Look, I don't want you to think
of it as just a business.

117
00:07:19,204 --> 00:07:23,511
I want you to see it
as our family's brand.

118
00:07:23,970 --> 00:07:26,076
That fashion stuff you studied...

119
00:07:26,101 --> 00:07:28,309
it's all about creating an image
people remember,

120
00:07:28,438 --> 00:07:30,986
something they keep
coming back to.

121
00:07:33,132 --> 00:07:34,179
Okay. Here's the deal.

122
00:07:35,826 --> 00:07:37,598
I'll give you six months.

123
00:07:37,623 --> 00:07:39,399
If, in those six months,

124
00:07:39,424 --> 00:07:42,194
you can make this course
profitable again,

125
00:07:43,231 --> 00:07:46,540
you can go back
and do whatever you want. Deal?

126
00:07:57,091 --> 00:07:58,198
But...

127
00:07:59,772 --> 00:08:03,224
if you can't do it in six months,

128
00:08:03,249 --> 00:08:05,005
I'll sell the golf course.

129
00:08:05,030 --> 00:08:07,794
And you won't be
going back there. Deal?

130
00:08:11,009 --> 00:08:12,063
Let's go.

131
00:08:15,844 --> 00:08:16,852
Dad!

132
00:08:17,207 --> 00:08:18,867
What does one
have to do with the other?

133
00:08:18,939 --> 00:08:22,122
If you won't even fight
for your own family,

134
00:08:22,147 --> 00:08:23,607
what will you fight for?

135
00:08:23,632 --> 00:08:25,737
- Still doesn't make sense, Dad.
- Huh?

136
00:08:27,526 --> 00:08:30,215
Look, I really do need your help.

137
00:08:30,240 --> 00:08:31,616
I need something fresh.

138
00:08:33,470 --> 00:08:36,718
An old-timer like me

139
00:08:36,743 --> 00:08:39,211
can't come up with fresh ideas
like you kids can.

140
00:08:39,378 --> 00:08:41,227
You get it, right? Come on.

141
00:08:45,563 --> 00:08:48,079
Dad! We're not done talking!

142
00:08:48,104 --> 00:08:51,904
What's that got to do with me?
I'm not finished!

143
00:08:52,107 --> 00:08:55,006
Dad! How does that
even make sense? Dad!

144
00:08:55,031 --> 00:08:57,355
Dad! Dad!

145
00:08:57,633 --> 00:09:00,432
What does that have to...
I'm not done talking!

146
00:09:00,457 --> 00:09:02,616
Dad! Dad!

147
00:09:07,466 --> 00:09:09,314
Why does it have to be me?

148
00:09:26,444 --> 00:09:28,416
Sit, sit, sit! Fabulous.

149
00:09:30,051 --> 00:09:33,425
Welcome back, Miss Nana,
all the way from Paris,

150
00:09:33,450 --> 00:09:36,208
to Bangkok City, Thailand!

151
00:09:36,233 --> 00:09:38,233
- Yay!
- Yay!

152
00:09:38,625 --> 00:09:40,301
Glasses up!

153
00:09:41,460 --> 00:09:43,548
Cheers, darling!

154
00:09:45,060 --> 00:09:50,308
Coming back in such a rush?
Something definitely happened.

155
00:09:50,333 --> 00:09:52,159
Ooh! Can I guess?

156
00:09:52,445 --> 00:09:55,429
- You're getting married!
- What?

157
00:09:55,705 --> 00:09:58,117
- Married?
- To who?

158
00:09:59,063 --> 00:10:02,183
What wedding? Dad called me
back to run the golf course.

159
00:10:02,995 --> 00:10:05,014
What's wrong
with your golf course?

160
00:10:05,039 --> 00:10:07,039
Why do you have to
run it yourself?

161
00:10:07,246 --> 00:10:09,745
Well... it's been losing money.

162
00:10:11,924 --> 00:10:13,638
Do you even know
anything about golf?

163
00:10:15,262 --> 00:10:18,519
Then just sell it.
That's a huge piece of land.

164
00:10:18,544 --> 00:10:21,760
I'm sure some property
developer would snap it up.

165
00:10:22,054 --> 00:10:25,366
I can't. Dad says the course
is part of our family brand.

166
00:10:25,391 --> 00:10:27,323
It's where
our family business began.

167
00:10:27,348 --> 00:10:29,284
If we can't even keep
our first business alive,

168
00:10:29,309 --> 00:10:30,855
we'll lose our credibility.

169
00:10:31,079 --> 00:10:33,368
Well, then you don't really
have a choice.

170
00:10:33,860 --> 00:10:35,657
Dad gave me six months.

171
00:10:35,682 --> 00:10:37,625
If I can turn things around,

172
00:10:37,650 --> 00:10:40,177
I get to go back
to my life in France.

173
00:10:42,506 --> 00:10:46,930
Nana, if there's anything
we can do, just say the word.

174
00:10:59,886 --> 00:11:02,185
Can I get a salted
caramel iced coffee?

175
00:11:02,210 --> 00:11:04,494
Extra sweet, please.
And only half a cup of ice.

176
00:11:04,519 --> 00:11:05,528
Sure.

177
00:11:05,553 --> 00:11:08,172
This place looks great.
How long have you been open?

178
00:11:08,251 --> 00:11:10,374
It's been three months
since I opened this place.

179
00:11:10,399 --> 00:11:13,353
And this is Pim's
fourth location, Nana.

180
00:11:13,378 --> 00:11:15,498
Wow, Pim. Look at you!

181
00:11:15,523 --> 00:11:17,975
This place broke even
in the first two months.

182
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,856
I couldn't believe it.

183
00:11:19,881 --> 00:11:22,001
Couldn't believe it
or couldn't wait to brag?

184
00:11:22,026 --> 00:11:24,026
- I was genuinely shocked!
- Sure.

185
00:11:25,439 --> 00:11:27,331
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

186
00:11:28,379 --> 00:11:29,593
Thanks.

187
00:11:30,636 --> 00:11:31,756
What about you, Aom?

188
00:11:33,357 --> 00:11:36,474
She has it easiest
out of all of us.

189
00:11:36,499 --> 00:11:38,954
She's married
and a full-time housewife.

190
00:11:38,979 --> 00:11:41,336
And she basically
names her own allowance.

191
00:11:41,766 --> 00:11:44,259
God, I'm jealous.

192
00:11:44,732 --> 00:11:47,161
I've probably got it the worst.

193
00:11:47,747 --> 00:11:49,621
I'm juggling condo projects,

194
00:11:49,646 --> 00:11:52,644
housing developments,
office buildings...

195
00:11:53,629 --> 00:11:58,346
All I see all day is bricks,
rocks, dirt, sand, and cement.

196
00:11:59,513 --> 00:12:02,088
And yet you still look
as gorgeous as ever, Meow.

197
00:12:02,123 --> 00:12:05,187
That's what skincare
is for, darling.

198
00:12:05,212 --> 00:12:06,401
True.

199
00:12:06,634 --> 00:12:07,880
What about you, Fahsai?

200
00:12:07,905 --> 00:12:10,451
Same old.
Still running my clothing store.

201
00:12:10,545 --> 00:12:12,347
Though I've been thinking of

202
00:12:12,372 --> 00:12:15,029
opening a cafe
to compete with Pim.

203
00:12:15,155 --> 00:12:18,094
Go for it, if you don't have
enough headaches already.

204
00:12:20,614 --> 00:12:23,599
Well, then let me
sponsor lunch today.

205
00:12:26,475 --> 00:12:31,735
Nana, you "sponsor" an event.

206
00:12:31,760 --> 00:12:34,610
You mean lunch is on you.

207
00:12:34,635 --> 00:12:37,925
Whatever. Lunch is on me, then.

208
00:12:37,950 --> 00:12:41,433
Don't be silly. This is my cafe.
I can afford to feed my friends.

209
00:12:41,458 --> 00:12:43,982
No way, Pim.
Business is business.

210
00:12:44,007 --> 00:12:48,506
Yes, Miss Moneybags.
You really haven't changed.

211
00:12:48,531 --> 00:12:51,357
Not one bit! Come on, cheers!

212
00:12:51,382 --> 00:12:54,207
- Again, again!
- To us!

213
00:13:09,521 --> 00:13:10,567
Hey, August.

214
00:13:10,592 --> 00:13:12,663
Dad wants to know
if you're coming home for dinner.

215
00:13:13,004 --> 00:13:15,222
Yeah. Tell him to wait for me.

216
00:13:16,793 --> 00:13:20,537
Oh, and about... Whoa, wait...

217
00:13:21,993 --> 00:13:25,765
Help! Somebody help!
Thief!

218
00:13:39,887 --> 00:13:40,900
What the hell?

219
00:14:18,777 --> 00:14:21,076
That's my phone.
Thank you so much.

220
00:14:21,862 --> 00:14:23,166
Are you okay?

221
00:14:24,462 --> 00:14:26,058
I'm fine. Thank you.

222
00:14:37,630 --> 00:14:40,733
- Excuse me!
- Nana! You're okay?

223
00:14:40,758 --> 00:14:42,312
Are you okay? Did you get hurt?

224
00:14:43,826 --> 00:14:45,944
- You okay?
- You're all right now, right?

225
00:15:21,302 --> 00:15:23,113
Why is it so dead around here?

226
00:15:25,208 --> 00:15:27,132
Where do I even start?

227
00:15:38,876 --> 00:15:43,083
Hmm. Nice grip.
And it signs like a dream.

228
00:15:52,201 --> 00:15:53,843
Hello, Miss Nana.

229
00:15:56,704 --> 00:15:57,720
Hello.

230
00:16:01,095 --> 00:16:03,836
Are you Dad's... you know?

231
00:16:03,861 --> 00:16:06,401
- Oh, no! I'm not!
- Nana, this is Belle.

232
00:16:07,887 --> 00:16:10,162
I thought you were
Mr. Sanchai's latest fling.

233
00:16:10,187 --> 00:16:12,219
I was about to tell you to run
for your life.

234
00:16:12,244 --> 00:16:13,785
He's so naggy and...

235
00:16:13,809 --> 00:16:15,525
You mean "nagging," Miss Nana?

236
00:16:16,572 --> 00:16:19,397
Yeah, that. Nagging,
grumpy, stingy,

237
00:16:19,422 --> 00:16:21,359
and he'll probably live forever.

238
00:16:21,383 --> 00:16:24,458
So if you're after his money,
you've got a long wait ahead.

239
00:16:25,233 --> 00:16:26,796
Okay, that's enough.

240
00:16:26,821 --> 00:16:29,217
I assigned Belle
to be your assistant.

241
00:16:29,309 --> 00:16:31,807
She was on the team that launched
our mining project in Ranong.

242
00:16:31,832 --> 00:16:33,396
Now that it's up and running,

243
00:16:33,421 --> 00:16:34,930
I brought her here to help you.

244
00:16:35,557 --> 00:16:38,165
I'm Belle.
But you can call me Bella.

245
00:16:38,190 --> 00:16:39,983
Whatever you need, Miss Nana,

246
00:16:40,008 --> 00:16:42,396
I'll make it happen.
You can count on me.

247
00:16:42,854 --> 00:16:44,798
I want to go back
to France tomorrow.

248
00:16:44,823 --> 00:16:46,214
Can you make that happen?

249
00:16:46,238 --> 00:16:47,341
- Oh!
- Hmm?

250
00:16:48,918 --> 00:16:50,033
Going straight for it, huh?

251
00:16:51,664 --> 00:16:53,299
Well, then...

252
00:16:54,149 --> 00:16:57,635
If you can make this golf course
profitable by this afternoon,

253
00:16:57,660 --> 00:17:00,711
I'll have a private jet
fly you straight back to France.

254
00:17:00,870 --> 00:17:03,070
Deal? It's settled, then.

255
00:17:16,382 --> 00:17:18,191
I've scheduled a meeting

256
00:17:18,216 --> 00:17:20,293
with all the department heads
this afternoon.

257
00:17:20,317 --> 00:17:22,172
So you can meet everyone
who runs each team.

258
00:17:22,197 --> 00:17:24,085
Okay. You know them all already?

259
00:17:24,110 --> 00:17:26,977
Yes. Mr. Sanchai had me start
a few months ago.

260
00:17:27,024 --> 00:17:29,451
Anything I need to do, should do,
or absolutely shouldn't do,

261
00:17:29,476 --> 00:17:30,545
just tell me.

262
00:17:30,569 --> 00:17:31,999
Let's just be friends, okay?

263
00:17:32,024 --> 00:17:35,501
Of course. So, what do you know
about our golf course?

264
00:17:35,693 --> 00:17:38,232
I know the name.
Goodwill Golf Club.

265
00:17:38,257 --> 00:17:40,102
Where Legacy Meets the Good.

266
00:17:40,126 --> 00:17:41,467
Nailed it.

267
00:17:42,366 --> 00:17:44,384
And I know we have 18 holes.

268
00:17:44,409 --> 00:17:47,465
Every standard golf course
has 18 holes, Miss Nana.

269
00:17:47,490 --> 00:17:49,468
I know Chef Queen's
food is amazing.

270
00:17:49,493 --> 00:17:51,653
I know we get fewer customers
during the rainy season.

271
00:17:51,678 --> 00:17:54,012
And I know our course is
one of the top ten in Thailand.

272
00:17:54,663 --> 00:17:56,663
You actually know
quite a lot, Miss Nana.

273
00:17:57,089 --> 00:17:58,216
Have you ever played?

274
00:17:59,423 --> 00:18:00,835
Of course. When we were kids,

275
00:18:00,860 --> 00:18:03,145
Dad used to bring August
and me here all the time.

276
00:18:03,601 --> 00:18:05,410
But back then...

277
00:18:09,235 --> 00:18:10,965
Yay!

278
00:18:26,860 --> 00:18:28,851
Gotcha! Pinchy crab!

279
00:18:29,764 --> 00:18:31,185
August!

280
00:18:31,631 --> 00:18:34,635
- Catch me if you can!
- Hey! Stop running!

281
00:18:35,206 --> 00:18:39,448
August! Stop right now!
Ow!

282
00:18:48,233 --> 00:18:49,896
Nana! Are you hurt?

283
00:18:51,622 --> 00:18:55,829
August, you can't play like that.
Look, Nana got hurt.

284
00:18:56,336 --> 00:18:58,705
Why don't we head back
to the clubhouse?

285
00:19:12,725 --> 00:19:13,915
August!

286
00:19:15,305 --> 00:19:16,385
Ow!

287
00:19:18,232 --> 00:19:19,968
Vee... it hurts.

288
00:19:19,993 --> 00:19:21,828
Nana, can you walk?

289
00:19:21,853 --> 00:19:24,026
If you can't,
I'll give you a piggyback ride.

290
00:19:40,378 --> 00:19:43,501
And after that, I never
set foot on the course again.

291
00:19:44,273 --> 00:19:46,758
I'm still mad at
that little brat.

292
00:19:47,592 --> 00:19:51,610
So basically, your golf skills
are... zero.

293
00:19:52,043 --> 00:19:54,042
Negative, even.

294
00:20:02,870 --> 00:20:05,959
I'm sure you're all aware of
the situation we're in.

295
00:20:05,984 --> 00:20:08,142
Things haven't exactly
been going well.

296
00:20:08,350 --> 00:20:10,111
You could just say
they're going terribly.

297
00:20:10,791 --> 00:20:14,222
Wow. Thank you,
my darling August,

298
00:20:14,247 --> 00:20:16,691
for making that painfully clear.

299
00:20:17,403 --> 00:20:19,895
But he's right.
That's why I've decided

300
00:20:19,920 --> 00:20:22,172
to put my eldest daughter, Nana,

301
00:20:22,197 --> 00:20:24,450
in charge of the golf course.

302
00:20:24,475 --> 00:20:28,480
I'm hoping she'll bring some
much-needed change around here.

303
00:20:29,690 --> 00:20:30,713
Applause, please.

304
00:20:37,279 --> 00:20:40,716
Hello, everyone. I look forward
to working with you all.

305
00:20:41,350 --> 00:20:46,436
Let me introduce you to
our department heads, Miss Nana.

306
00:20:46,646 --> 00:20:48,416
Almost everyone's here today.

307
00:20:48,441 --> 00:20:51,847
The accounting team is busy
closing the books,

308
00:20:51,872 --> 00:20:54,313
and a few of our golf pros
are with clients.

309
00:20:55,361 --> 00:20:58,647
Starting over here, we have
March, our general manager.

310
00:20:58,672 --> 00:21:01,746
Chef Queen, our executive chef
and clubhouse manager,

311
00:21:01,771 --> 00:21:04,233
who oversees all food
and beverage operations.

312
00:21:04,478 --> 00:21:07,903
Eak, our head starter,
and Mam, our head caddie.

313
00:21:07,928 --> 00:21:11,866
And in the back is Key,
our head of marketing.

314
00:21:12,247 --> 00:21:16,250
Now, let me give you a quick
overview of the golf course.

315
00:21:28,983 --> 00:21:31,174
Belle, sweetie.
Come into my office for a sec.

316
00:21:33,630 --> 00:21:34,852
Yes, Miss Nana.

317
00:21:37,082 --> 00:21:39,467
I've been looking over
the numbers from accounting.

318
00:21:40,269 --> 00:21:41,993
Our revenue keeps dropping.

319
00:21:42,082 --> 00:21:44,718
So why are we spending more

320
00:21:44,743 --> 00:21:48,742
on fertilizer and turf chemicals
every year?

321
00:21:49,442 --> 00:21:51,491
Maybe the prices have gone up?

322
00:21:52,213 --> 00:21:55,350
Not by much. I already
checked the past prices.

323
00:21:55,375 --> 00:21:58,695
What's even stranger
is how often we're ordering them.

324
00:21:59,795 --> 00:22:02,168
Some months, three or four times.

325
00:22:03,232 --> 00:22:04,890
Who's usually in charge of this?

326
00:22:09,366 --> 00:22:10,972
I'll take care of the paperwork.

327
00:22:11,655 --> 00:22:14,766
Don't worry. Just keep
everything business as usual.

328
00:22:15,406 --> 00:22:16,698
Like nothing ever happened.

329
00:22:18,737 --> 00:22:20,086
And don't ask too many questions.

330
00:22:27,810 --> 00:22:29,553
Oh, March. You're still here?

331
00:22:30,092 --> 00:22:31,791
You're usually gone by three.

332
00:22:33,977 --> 00:22:36,416
What about you, Belle?
Aren't you going home?

333
00:22:36,578 --> 00:22:37,697
It's already six.

334
00:22:38,134 --> 00:22:39,784
I'm the new boss's assistant.

335
00:22:39,809 --> 00:22:42,580
How can I leave before
the boss does? Right?

336
00:22:44,444 --> 00:22:48,752
True. Our new boss
sure is fired up.

337
00:22:49,707 --> 00:22:52,142
Oh, she certainly is.

338
00:22:52,167 --> 00:22:54,878
Better be careful. That kind of
fire could burn you to a crisp.

339
00:22:58,441 --> 00:22:59,762
Excuse me.

340
00:23:20,130 --> 00:23:22,303
Miss Nana,
are you holding up okay?

341
00:23:22,328 --> 00:23:25,057
- Of course.
- You sure?

342
00:23:25,082 --> 00:23:26,576
I want to learn how to play golf.

343
00:23:27,279 --> 00:23:29,493
Aren't you afraid August
will come pick on you again?

344
00:23:30,660 --> 00:23:33,495
Let him try that again.
I'll get him back this time.

345
00:23:33,746 --> 00:23:35,848
So why the sudden
interest in golf?

346
00:23:36,396 --> 00:23:38,316
If I'm going to
run a golf course,

347
00:23:38,369 --> 00:23:41,257
I should at least know
what makes the game fun.

348
00:23:43,122 --> 00:23:44,740
Find me someone to teach me.

349
00:23:45,097 --> 00:23:48,470
Find someone to teach me.

350
00:23:50,354 --> 00:23:53,706
Here you go.
Take your pick, Miss Nana.

351
00:24:02,909 --> 00:24:04,165
Wait... it's her.

352
00:24:05,459 --> 00:24:06,985
I want her to teach me.

353
00:24:07,558 --> 00:24:09,512
Hmm... Pro Venus.

354
00:24:10,059 --> 00:24:11,497
I love her.

355
00:24:12,132 --> 00:24:13,148
Excuse me?

356
00:24:14,190 --> 00:24:16,343
Her name! Venus.

357
00:24:17,010 --> 00:24:18,764
The goddess of love.

358
00:24:21,902 --> 00:24:24,011
Like this, Pro Vee?

359
00:24:26,107 --> 00:24:28,107
Here. Let me show you.

360
00:24:42,106 --> 00:24:43,262
Hold it like this.

361
00:24:56,910 --> 00:24:59,538
Why are you blushing, Nana?

362
00:25:07,828 --> 00:25:10,756
I'm just shy around you.

363
00:25:30,619 --> 00:25:32,781
What perfume
are you wearing, Nana?

364
00:25:33,828 --> 00:25:34,894
You smell amazing.

365
00:25:45,815 --> 00:25:50,083
All right. Let's work
on your backswing. Like this.

366
00:26:06,960 --> 00:26:11,804
Belle, sweetie.
Mission number one starts now.

367
00:26:18,607 --> 00:26:21,945
♪ Everyone can tell
by the way you stare ♪

368
00:26:22,684 --> 00:26:24,417
♪ Sneaking little looks
when I'm unaware ♪

369
00:26:24,442 --> 00:26:28,536
♪ It's plain to see ♪

370
00:26:28,561 --> 00:26:30,238
♪ I know exactly
what you think of me ♪

371
00:26:30,263 --> 00:26:34,377
♪ First to watch my stories
every time ♪

372
00:26:34,402 --> 00:26:36,071
♪ You remember
every fave of mine ♪

373
00:26:36,096 --> 00:26:39,875
♪ Everywhere I go,
you're by my side ♪

374
00:26:39,900 --> 00:26:41,900
♪ Don't tell me
there's nothing on your mind ♪

375
00:26:41,925 --> 00:26:44,785
♪ So when are you
gonna say the words? ♪

376
00:26:44,810 --> 00:26:46,613
♪ Don't keep me waiting
till it hurts ♪

377
00:26:46,638 --> 00:26:49,441
♪ The way you act,
I know you're into me ♪

378
00:26:49,466 --> 00:26:52,395
♪ That racing heart
gives you away so easily ♪

379
00:26:52,420 --> 00:26:56,161
♪ But I'll play clueless,
just wait and see ♪

380
00:26:56,186 --> 00:26:58,186
♪ I wanna hear you say it to me ♪

381
00:26:58,211 --> 00:27:01,151
♪ Giving me signs,
so why still wait? ♪

382
00:27:01,176 --> 00:27:04,558
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

383
00:27:04,583 --> 00:27:09,333
♪ How long will you keep
playing so tough? ♪

384
00:27:09,358 --> 00:27:11,358
♪ Or should I be the one
to call your bluff? ♪

385
00:27:33,080 --> 00:27:35,690
Listen, Nana. You can do this.

386
00:27:35,715 --> 00:27:39,486
Operation Save the Golf Course is
going to be a smashing success.

387
00:27:39,511 --> 00:27:42,578
Then you'll be back
living your best life in France,

388
00:27:42,603 --> 00:27:45,972
chasing your dreams down
a runway flooded with spotlights,

389
00:27:45,997 --> 00:27:47,997
not a fairway
flooded with UV rays.

390
00:27:48,364 --> 00:27:53,636
Which means tomorrow, you get to
dress up and go see Pro Venus.

391
00:27:56,616 --> 00:27:58,479
Pro Venus...
Just thinking about her...

392
00:28:01,463 --> 00:28:02,725
Pro Venus...

393
00:28:43,088 --> 00:28:46,161
I'm late! I'm late!

394
00:28:49,024 --> 00:28:50,856
Why am I taking the blanket?

395
00:28:59,476 --> 00:29:02,551
Two hours and 48 minutes
from home to the course?

396
00:29:04,443 --> 00:29:07,533
It's 7:30.
I'm meeting her at nine.

397
00:29:08,492 --> 00:29:11,683
Oh my God. Oh my God!

398
00:29:11,708 --> 00:29:16,624
Shower! Bathroom, bathroom...
Where's the bathroom?

399
00:29:17,347 --> 00:29:21,412
Where's the shower?
No... the bathroom's this way.

400
00:29:21,437 --> 00:29:24,953
This way, this way...
Forget it!

401
00:29:37,896 --> 00:29:38,964
Good morning.

402
00:29:41,225 --> 00:29:44,130
Sorry! I had no idea
it was this far.

403
00:29:44,155 --> 00:29:45,661
And the traffic was awful.

404
00:29:45,686 --> 00:29:47,747
Where do you live?
Don't you get traffic?

405
00:29:47,771 --> 00:29:50,330
- I live on the course.
- On the course?

406
00:29:51,413 --> 00:29:55,365
- Which hole?
- No. In the staff housing.

407
00:29:55,678 --> 00:29:57,146
Oh...

408
00:29:57,171 --> 00:29:59,388
We should hurry.
Pro Vee's been waiting a while.

409
00:29:59,530 --> 00:30:00,578
Let's go.

410
00:30:25,654 --> 00:30:27,836
- Is that her?
- Yes.

411
00:30:38,811 --> 00:30:41,447
Pro Vee, Miss Nana is here.

412
00:30:42,239 --> 00:30:44,305
Miss Nana, this is Pro Venus.

413
00:30:44,330 --> 00:30:46,717
She'll be teaching you golf.

414
00:30:47,709 --> 00:30:49,941
It's so nice to see you again.

415
00:30:51,665 --> 00:30:54,118
Shall we get started?
You're an hour late.

416
00:30:56,087 --> 00:30:57,158
Right...

417
00:31:02,430 --> 00:31:03,961
You've played before, right?

418
00:31:04,390 --> 00:31:06,390
- Yes.
- Then show me your drive.

419
00:31:23,414 --> 00:31:26,972
Don't bother looking.
You missed it.

420
00:31:42,507 --> 00:31:43,621
Missed again.

421
00:31:47,487 --> 00:31:51,549
Fix your grip. Bring your right
hand in. Finger here.

422
00:31:53,790 --> 00:31:54,878
Closer.

423
00:31:56,231 --> 00:31:59,383
What are you looking at?
Focus. Watch.

424
00:32:01,417 --> 00:32:02,425
Hold it like this.

425
00:32:04,546 --> 00:32:05,963
Now show me your backswing.

426
00:32:09,249 --> 00:32:10,967
Keep your left arm straight.

427
00:32:12,530 --> 00:32:14,620
Take it all the way back.
Then swing down.

428
00:32:19,770 --> 00:32:21,053
Mm-hmm. Give it a try.

429
00:32:23,191 --> 00:32:24,993
It's so hot.

430
00:32:25,215 --> 00:32:27,893
- I didn't even put on sunscreen.
- Try it.

431
00:32:28,600 --> 00:32:30,140
I'm thirsty.

432
00:32:30,793 --> 00:32:31,873
Backswing.

433
00:32:33,922 --> 00:32:36,274
Left arm straight.
Turn your hips.

434
00:32:41,123 --> 00:32:42,147
Like this?

435
00:32:43,361 --> 00:32:44,433
Keep your head still.

436
00:32:50,302 --> 00:32:51,840
I thought you said
you'd played before.

437
00:32:52,994 --> 00:32:56,017
I did. When I was little, but...

438
00:32:56,042 --> 00:32:58,465
Then a crab pinched your finger,

439
00:32:58,553 --> 00:33:02,222
and you got smacked in the face
with a golf club. So you quit.

440
00:33:02,247 --> 00:33:06,131
How did you know a crab
pinched me when I was little?

441
00:33:07,117 --> 00:33:09,657
Wait... are you...

442
00:33:10,005 --> 00:33:11,747
Yes. It was me.

443
00:33:17,424 --> 00:33:19,568
I can't believe it.

444
00:33:19,593 --> 00:33:21,727
Fairway of Love.

445
00:33:21,752 --> 00:33:23,752
Golf brings hearts together.

446
00:33:28,747 --> 00:33:29,810
What's wrong with you?

447
00:33:31,160 --> 00:33:34,597
Oh! Nothing.

448
00:33:35,188 --> 00:33:38,580
It's so nice
that we found each other again.

449
00:33:38,605 --> 00:33:42,779
Then you can teach me like
you did when we were kids, right?

450
00:33:44,186 --> 00:33:46,992
I only teach people
who are genuinely committed.

451
00:33:47,017 --> 00:33:49,169
You were an hour late
to your very first lesson.

452
00:33:49,194 --> 00:33:52,402
By my standards,
you've already failed.

453
00:33:53,606 --> 00:33:55,829
But Pro Vee, the traffic
from my house was...

454
00:33:55,854 --> 00:33:57,734
I'll give you one more chance.

455
00:33:58,098 --> 00:34:01,378
I'll teach you
if you can meet one condition.

456
00:34:02,338 --> 00:34:03,727
What condition?

457
00:34:07,255 --> 00:34:10,487
The seventh hole here
is a par five.

458
00:34:10,667 --> 00:34:14,332
That means you're expected
to finish it in five strokes.

459
00:34:14,789 --> 00:34:17,488
You have two weeks to practice.

460
00:34:17,513 --> 00:34:19,305
You need to finish that hole

461
00:34:19,349 --> 00:34:22,129
no more than
two strokes over par.

462
00:34:23,343 --> 00:34:26,180
- Choo-choo!
- What are you doing?

463
00:34:26,205 --> 00:34:27,777
Hole seven, par five.

464
00:34:27,802 --> 00:34:29,928
And you're giving me
two extra strokes.

465
00:34:29,953 --> 00:34:31,265
That's a double bogey.

466
00:34:31,289 --> 00:34:34,609
Bogey-bogey! Choo-choo!

467
00:34:34,634 --> 00:34:36,110
Was I supposed to laugh at that?

468
00:34:42,333 --> 00:34:44,405
Pass my test,

469
00:34:44,430 --> 00:34:45,952
and I'll teach you.

470
00:34:47,075 --> 00:34:51,065
Two weeks?
That's fourteen whole days. Easy.

471
00:34:51,090 --> 00:34:55,032
I can only teach you the basics
twice a week.

472
00:34:55,057 --> 00:34:57,001
The rest, you'll have to
practice on your own.

473
00:34:57,226 --> 00:34:58,766
- But...
- No buts.

474
00:35:00,967 --> 00:35:02,217
Fine.

475
00:35:03,067 --> 00:35:06,814
But why two weeks?

476
00:35:07,006 --> 00:35:10,086
Let's just say
I have my reasons.

477
00:35:13,832 --> 00:35:16,978
I'd like you to come work
at my golf course.

478
00:35:17,987 --> 00:35:20,045
Thank you, Ms. Yupadee.

479
00:35:20,070 --> 00:35:23,070
But I'm happy where I am.

480
00:35:25,053 --> 00:35:29,393
I'll be straight with you.
I've admired you for a long time.

481
00:35:30,411 --> 00:35:32,597
Ever since you were
a junior golfer.

482
00:35:34,478 --> 00:35:35,815
Think it over carefully.

483
00:35:36,544 --> 00:35:40,017
You know what things
are like over there.

484
00:35:40,534 --> 00:35:45,123
I heard Mr. Sanchai's
run out of ideas

485
00:35:45,599 --> 00:35:47,725
and had to put
his daughter in charge.

486
00:35:50,283 --> 00:35:51,981
Who knows how long that'll last?

487
00:35:56,510 --> 00:35:58,609
If you come work at my course,

488
00:36:00,207 --> 00:36:02,683
I'll raise your coaching fee
by 30 percent.

489
00:36:04,403 --> 00:36:07,433
Well, actually...

490
00:36:09,929 --> 00:36:11,767
You don't have to answer me now.

491
00:36:12,878 --> 00:36:14,298
Take some time to think about it.

492
00:36:21,892 --> 00:36:23,777
I'll give you two weeks.

493
00:36:43,562 --> 00:36:45,347
This is the executive residence.

494
00:36:45,372 --> 00:36:46,942
No one's stayed here
in a long time.

495
00:36:46,966 --> 00:36:48,258
But don't worry.

496
00:36:48,282 --> 00:36:50,446
I already had the place
cleaned from top to bottom.

497
00:36:53,471 --> 00:36:55,006
No ghosts, right?

498
00:36:55,031 --> 00:36:56,633
- No...
- No ghosts?

499
00:36:56,658 --> 00:36:58,658
No idea. Boo!

500
00:36:59,066 --> 00:37:00,312
Belle!

501
00:37:00,681 --> 00:37:03,220
Don't worry.
I live just behind here.

502
00:37:03,466 --> 00:37:05,928
If you see a ghost,
just call me.

503
00:37:05,953 --> 00:37:07,718
Or scream my name.
I'll hear you.

504
00:37:07,743 --> 00:37:08,837
Belle!

505
00:37:10,507 --> 00:37:11,992
I should get going.

506
00:37:17,784 --> 00:37:22,310
Come on, Nana. It's only
six months. Piece of cake.

507
00:37:30,091 --> 00:37:31,766
I can do this.

508
00:38:26,530 --> 00:38:30,541
Pro Vee! Pro Vee, wait!

509
00:38:31,126 --> 00:38:33,721
How nice!
We live so close to each other.

510
00:38:34,570 --> 00:38:36,715
Want to get breakfast together?

511
00:38:36,740 --> 00:38:38,382
I'm craving rice porridge.

512
00:38:38,406 --> 00:38:40,425
What do you usually
have for breakfast?

513
00:38:43,111 --> 00:38:44,280
Pro Vee?

514
00:38:45,631 --> 00:38:48,535
Pro Vee! Pro Vee...

515
00:38:55,372 --> 00:38:57,588
Bring your arms parallel
to the ground again.

516
00:38:57,715 --> 00:39:01,073
The main thing is to keep
your core

517
00:39:01,098 --> 00:39:03,550
and your arms moving together.

518
00:39:17,349 --> 00:39:21,053
Oh! Sorry, Mr. Sanchai.

519
00:39:21,452 --> 00:39:23,922
Come on, Pro Vee.
No need to be so formal with me.

520
00:39:24,461 --> 00:39:26,846
What brings you out here, Uncle?

521
00:39:28,078 --> 00:39:30,705
I came to watch
my little one practice.

522
00:39:34,086 --> 00:39:35,587
Mm. Not bad.

523
00:39:36,571 --> 00:39:39,024
Anyway, take good care
of her for me.

524
00:39:39,049 --> 00:39:40,549
- Of course.
- Thanks.

525
00:40:09,806 --> 00:40:12,583
March, I've been going through

526
00:40:12,608 --> 00:40:14,444
our closing statements
and purchase orders.

527
00:40:14,650 --> 00:40:17,303
A few of the numbers
look a little unusual.

528
00:40:17,328 --> 00:40:19,732
If anything looks strange,
just ask me, Nana.

529
00:40:20,248 --> 00:40:23,164
Our estimated monthly use
of consumable supplies,

530
00:40:23,189 --> 00:40:25,962
like fertilizer and herbicide,

531
00:40:25,987 --> 00:40:29,165
fungicide and golf balls,
based on last year's figures...

532
00:40:29,190 --> 00:40:31,792
why do the actual order amounts
vary so much?

533
00:40:31,872 --> 00:40:34,756
Hmm. If I remember correctly,

534
00:40:34,781 --> 00:40:37,710
it probably depends
on the weather at the time.

535
00:40:38,276 --> 00:40:40,199
Some months are hotter,
some are cooler,

536
00:40:40,224 --> 00:40:43,085
and some are more humid.
That's probably why.

537
00:40:43,110 --> 00:40:46,808
I'll be straight with you.
I've admired you for a long time.

538
00:40:47,455 --> 00:40:48,883
So we keep extras in stock.

539
00:40:48,908 --> 00:40:50,463
Speaking of weather,

540
00:40:50,488 --> 00:40:53,542
don't we only have
one season here? Hot?

541
00:40:54,850 --> 00:40:57,319
You're pretty funny, Nana.

542
00:40:58,058 --> 00:41:00,591
Anything else you want to ask?

543
00:41:00,616 --> 00:41:02,713
I have to rush to a meeting.

544
00:41:04,042 --> 00:41:05,661
I actually have tons
more questions,

545
00:41:05,686 --> 00:41:09,615
but I'll save them
for another day. Thank you.

546
00:41:30,499 --> 00:41:34,547
These veggies look amazing.
This curry's gonna be so good.

547
00:41:37,140 --> 00:41:39,140
Meow! Meow!

548
00:41:39,950 --> 00:41:43,755
A cat? Since when
do I have a cat in my kitchen?

549
00:41:44,918 --> 00:41:46,948
Meow! Meow!

550
00:41:46,973 --> 00:41:51,044
Where'd that cat come from?
I know I closed the kitchen.

551
00:41:56,975 --> 00:41:58,411
Woof! Woof!

552
00:41:59,404 --> 00:42:02,129
A dog? There's a dog in here too?

553
00:42:03,535 --> 00:42:06,467
Did it come after that cat?

554
00:42:06,492 --> 00:42:10,183
Shoo! Out!
Don't play around in my kitchen!

555
00:42:10,379 --> 00:42:12,790
Go on! Shoo!

556
00:42:13,434 --> 00:42:17,905
Cats and dogs now?
Is nobody watching this kitchen?

557
00:42:18,360 --> 00:42:20,757
Ooh, that smells good.

558
00:42:24,935 --> 00:42:26,550
Ooh-ooh! Aah-aah!

559
00:42:26,836 --> 00:42:30,356
A monkey? How the hell
did a monkey get in here?

560
00:42:30,882 --> 00:42:33,367
This is a kitchen, not a zoo!

561
00:42:33,714 --> 00:42:37,053
At this rate, a python's gonna
show up and strangle me next.

562
00:42:37,078 --> 00:42:39,323
I'll be dead! Go!

563
00:42:39,348 --> 00:42:42,536
Not in here, sweetie.
Everybody out! Shoo!

564
00:42:42,623 --> 00:42:45,430
God, now I'm paranoid.

565
00:42:45,547 --> 00:42:48,249
Meow! Meow!
Where are you?

566
00:42:49,055 --> 00:42:50,198
Jeez...

567
00:42:51,383 --> 00:42:55,067
Go on! Get out!

568
00:43:00,292 --> 00:43:04,568
- Boo!
- Aah! Miss Nana! You scared me!

569
00:43:04,593 --> 00:43:07,667
I'm hungry! I'm hungry!
Can I eat you?

570
00:43:07,692 --> 00:43:09,874
Oh, fine, eat me!
God, you scared me!

571
00:43:09,899 --> 00:43:11,668
You're too big for this!

572
00:43:11,693 --> 00:43:13,425
Why are you still
acting like a kid?

573
00:43:13,449 --> 00:43:15,928
Aww, there, there.
Don't be scared, Queen.

574
00:43:15,953 --> 00:43:18,697
Why didn't you tell the staff
you were coming in here?

575
00:43:18,722 --> 00:43:20,633
Just tell them
if you need something.

576
00:43:20,658 --> 00:43:23,229
You'll get all dirty
in the kitchen.

577
00:43:23,680 --> 00:43:25,767
Dirty? I'll wipe it off.
Smelly? I'll shower.

578
00:43:25,792 --> 00:43:28,702
Oh, aren't you adorable?

579
00:43:28,727 --> 00:43:32,648
What brings Your Highness here?
How may I be of service?

580
00:43:32,680 --> 00:43:35,629
I'm starving.
I got up early to practice golf,

581
00:43:35,654 --> 00:43:38,201
and I still have another lesson
with Pro Vee this evening.

582
00:43:38,226 --> 00:43:40,925
- Feed me, Queen. I'm starving.
- Exhausting, huh?

583
00:43:41,371 --> 00:43:42,458
What do you want?

584
00:43:43,942 --> 00:43:47,217
Anything.
Everything you make is delicious.

585
00:43:47,242 --> 00:43:49,990
Well, aren't you sweet?

586
00:43:50,015 --> 00:43:52,565
All right,
I'll whip something up.

587
00:43:52,590 --> 00:43:55,529
But you need to wait outside.

588
00:43:55,554 --> 00:43:57,870
It's hot, it smells,
and the floor can get slippery.

589
00:43:57,895 --> 00:44:00,542
Go on, sit outside.
I'll bring you something.

590
00:44:00,567 --> 00:44:02,313
- Rawr!
- Oh!

591
00:44:02,463 --> 00:44:06,031
You're all grown up,
and you're still such a child.

592
00:44:06,406 --> 00:44:07,438
Good grief...

593
00:44:08,599 --> 00:44:14,777
Here it comes!
Food's here!

594
00:44:14,802 --> 00:44:17,950
Food's here!

595
00:44:18,021 --> 00:44:19,953
Ta-da!

596
00:44:19,978 --> 00:44:22,415
Wow, that looks amazing!

597
00:44:22,440 --> 00:44:25,947
Stir-fried noodles with gravy,
no shrimpy!

598
00:44:26,887 --> 00:44:30,153
How come there's no shrimp?
Did you run out?

599
00:44:30,178 --> 00:44:32,638
Or are we cutting costs
to save the golf course?

600
00:44:32,663 --> 00:44:35,030
Oh, listen to you!

601
00:44:35,055 --> 00:44:36,910
If I put shrimp in there,

602
00:44:36,935 --> 00:44:39,556
someone around here wouldn't
be going to golf lessons.

603
00:44:39,581 --> 00:44:43,345
We'd be carrying you
straight to the hospital instead.

604
00:44:43,370 --> 00:44:44,935
Good memory, Queen.

605
00:44:44,960 --> 00:44:47,930
Of course I remember, Miss.
It was horrifying!

606
00:44:48,210 --> 00:44:49,847
You don't remember any of it,

607
00:44:49,872 --> 00:44:52,896
but everyone here does.
You accidentally ate shrimp,

608
00:44:52,921 --> 00:44:57,089
and your face swelled up
and turned bright red.

609
00:44:57,114 --> 00:45:01,061
We had to rush you
to the hospital. Terrifying!

610
00:45:02,720 --> 00:45:07,322
Mmm! This is so good, Queen.

611
00:45:09,726 --> 00:45:12,933
Too bad more people
don't get to taste your cooking.

612
00:45:13,555 --> 00:45:17,137
You know, I was convinced

613
00:45:17,162 --> 00:45:19,956
my gravy noodles
were the best in the world.

614
00:45:19,981 --> 00:45:22,267
I want more people to try it.

615
00:45:22,649 --> 00:45:26,883
But lately, this golf course
has been completely dead.

616
00:45:26,908 --> 00:45:28,908
All I do is...

617
00:45:29,539 --> 00:45:33,031
sit around swatting mosquitoes
in the kitchen.

618
00:45:33,056 --> 00:45:35,083
Don't sigh like that, Queen.

619
00:45:35,108 --> 00:45:38,077
I'm back now
to turn this place around

620
00:45:38,102 --> 00:45:40,102
and bring it back to life.

621
00:45:40,387 --> 00:45:42,977
Before you know it,

622
00:45:43,002 --> 00:45:47,604
you'll be chopping, slicing,
stir-frying, frying...

623
00:45:47,650 --> 00:45:50,304
so busy you won't even be
able to keep up with the orders.

624
00:45:50,329 --> 00:45:52,233
That busy, huh?

625
00:45:52,258 --> 00:45:56,736
I'm ready! Bring on
the customers. Bam, bam!

626
00:45:56,768 --> 00:45:59,860
I'm ready. Bam, bam!
I'll cook. Bam, bam!

627
00:46:01,085 --> 00:46:06,210
Oh! Miss Nana, what time
is your lesson with Pro Vee?

628
00:46:09,456 --> 00:46:12,723
- Hmm...
- Oh, no.

629
00:46:13,032 --> 00:46:16,519
Pro Vee is extremely strict
about discipline and punctuality.

630
00:46:16,544 --> 00:46:18,472
I was already late
on the first day.

631
00:46:18,497 --> 00:46:19,817
What?

632
00:46:19,848 --> 00:46:21,758
You can't do that, Miss Nana!

633
00:46:21,783 --> 00:46:24,998
But from now on,
I promise I won't be late again.

634
00:46:25,531 --> 00:46:27,398
- Promise?
- Promise.

635
00:46:28,536 --> 00:46:30,536
Good.

636
00:46:31,254 --> 00:46:32,943
Now eat, eat!

637
00:46:39,577 --> 00:46:43,002
- Mmm. Delicious, right?
- Delicious.

638
00:46:43,027 --> 00:46:45,485
Oh, no, no. Not like that.

639
00:46:45,510 --> 00:46:50,309
If it's really good,
you have to say, "De-li-cious!"

640
00:46:50,923 --> 00:46:52,339
De-li-cious!

641
00:46:56,260 --> 00:46:59,931
See those greens?
That's not Chinese kale.

642
00:47:00,138 --> 00:47:01,258
What is it?

643
00:47:01,283 --> 00:47:03,171
Grass from the golf course.

644
00:47:03,222 --> 00:47:05,929
- Nice and tender.
- Queen!

645
00:47:06,256 --> 00:47:10,013
- I'm serious. Kidding!
- Queen!

646
00:47:10,038 --> 00:47:11,854
Eat, eat!

647
00:47:25,356 --> 00:47:27,816
- A stomach marches on its army.
- Huh?

648
00:47:28,334 --> 00:47:29,836
You know, an army marches.

649
00:47:29,861 --> 00:47:32,490
If you're going to work hard,
you need to eat first.

650
00:47:32,568 --> 00:47:35,818
"An army marches on its stomach."
At least get the saying right.

651
00:47:39,630 --> 00:47:41,960
I had Chef Queen
make us some sandwiches.

652
00:47:41,985 --> 00:47:44,613
Want one? Her food is amazing.

653
00:47:44,638 --> 00:47:46,085
Even a simple sandwich tastes...

654
00:47:49,985 --> 00:47:51,113
Hey! Watch out!

655
00:48:00,646 --> 00:48:01,772
Are you okay?

656
00:48:06,756 --> 00:48:07,790
Come on, up you go.

657
00:48:12,119 --> 00:48:13,151
Careful.

658
00:48:13,676 --> 00:48:16,845
Thanks. Here's your sandwich.

659
00:48:18,641 --> 00:48:19,816
Thanks.

660
00:48:28,207 --> 00:48:31,645
Exactly, Aom. I accidentally
stepped on a golf ball.

661
00:48:32,681 --> 00:48:35,276
Oh, shut up.
I did not stage that!

662
00:48:38,059 --> 00:48:39,352
Gotta go, Aom.

663
00:48:39,376 --> 00:48:42,282
Looks like I have
an uninvited nighttime visitor.

664
00:49:23,645 --> 00:49:24,694
Oh!

665
00:49:29,399 --> 00:49:30,418
What is it?

666
00:50:04,034 --> 00:50:06,940
Who told you
I'm not scared of geckos?

667
00:50:07,178 --> 00:50:09,982
Wait, you're scared of them too?

668
00:50:35,585 --> 00:50:38,552
There! Pro Vee, I see it!

669
00:50:38,990 --> 00:50:40,784
What are we going
to do with the little guy?

670
00:50:41,365 --> 00:50:45,057
Don't hurt him, though.
I feel bad for him.

671
00:50:46,249 --> 00:50:49,612
Then let's try
to chase him out of the room.

672
00:50:50,716 --> 00:50:51,803
Okay.

673
00:51:34,292 --> 00:51:35,962
I think he's gone.

674
00:51:35,987 --> 00:51:38,313
Yeah. I think so.

675
00:52:00,615 --> 00:52:04,072
You can't do this. I've helped
Uncle run this course for years.

676
00:52:04,445 --> 00:52:06,445
Besides, we're family.

677
00:52:06,470 --> 00:52:09,997
Exactly, March. Family shouldn't
steal from family.

678
00:52:10,022 --> 00:52:12,992
I'll shut this course down
and wipe its name off the map.

679
00:52:13,017 --> 00:52:17,712
The heart of golf is L-O-V-E.

680
00:52:18,337 --> 00:52:20,804
Thanks for saying
you love me, Pro Vee.

681
00:52:21,044 --> 00:52:22,195
What?

682
00:52:22,250 --> 00:52:25,966
I'm curious what golf pros do

683
00:52:25,991 --> 00:52:27,229
on their days off.

684
00:52:27,254 --> 00:52:29,868
Can I tag along with you
for a day?

685
00:52:32,030 --> 00:52:36,485
♪ Do you know which way to go? ♪

686
00:52:37,321 --> 00:52:42,142
♪ To get us closer to our goal ♪

687
00:52:42,311 --> 00:52:46,956
♪ Together, we'll race
toward the line ♪

688
00:52:47,481 --> 00:52:52,031
♪ Chasing the dream
that's yours and mine ♪

689
00:52:52,605 --> 00:52:57,778
♪ In the end,
I know we'll make it there ♪

690
00:52:57,803 --> 00:53:01,923
♪ Just one rule
for you and me to share ♪

691
00:53:02,679 --> 00:53:05,778
♪ Promise you'll stay
close to me ♪

692
00:53:05,803 --> 00:53:08,328
♪ Hold me in your arms
so tenderly ♪

693
00:53:08,353 --> 00:53:14,023
♪ I've never bowed
to anyone in sight ♪

694
00:53:14,060 --> 00:53:17,234
♪ But for you,
I'd surrender without a fight ♪

695
00:53:17,259 --> 00:53:21,705
♪ Just take my hand
and hold it tight ♪

696
00:53:23,329 --> 00:53:26,419
♪ And walk with me
along the way ♪

697
00:53:26,444 --> 00:53:29,025
♪ No matter what it takes
to win someday ♪

698
00:53:29,050 --> 00:53:34,615
♪ Sometimes this tender heart
may despair ♪

699
00:53:34,826 --> 00:53:37,907
♪ But tell me,
why should we care? ♪

700
00:53:37,932 --> 00:53:40,305
♪ When all we need
is love that's fair ♪

701
00:53:40,330 --> 00:53:44,152
♪ In a love we share,
no one has to win or lose ♪

702
00:53:46,163 --> 00:53:51,033
♪ Let my heart answer anew ♪

703
00:53:51,389 --> 00:53:56,465
♪ A thousand rounds,
it'd still choose you ♪

704
00:53:56,490 --> 00:54:01,019
♪ One look in your eyes
is all I need ♪

705
00:54:01,311 --> 00:54:04,873
♪ Oh, baby. I trust your sweet. ♪
